\subsection{Research attempt}
\paragraph{Model, date and investigated scope.}
OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (configured model \texttt{gpt-6-astra}), ultra reasoning; generated 11 October 2026. Proved the density-zero consequence of variance control and explicitly falsified its upgrade to all-index equidistribution; no eigenfunction counterexample or QUE proof.

\paragraph{Sources and literature check.}
Read the supplied definition, catalogue wording, source qualifications and reference entries for 30004023. The historical source/context and inherited status are retained; no fresh literature or novelty certification is claimed. No external theorem is used without proof in this attempt; explicit model assumptions are distinguished from facts about the source model.

\paragraph{Testing the density-one route.} A common attempted upgrade starts from an averaged variance estimate for a fixed observable. Abstractly, let \(a_j\ge0\) be its squared equidistribution error and suppose \(N^{-1}\sum_{j\le N}a_j\to0\). For every \(\delta>0\), the number of \(j\le N\) with \(a_j\ge\delta\) is at most \(\delta^{-1}\sum_{j\le N}a_j=o(N)\). This establishes a zero-density exceptional set for each fixed threshold, but not its absence.
\paragraph{An exact obstruction to the upgrade.} Set \(a_j=1\) when \(j\) is a perfect square and zero otherwise. Then
\[
 \frac1N\sum_{j\le N}a_j=\frac{\lfloor\sqrt N\rfloor}{N}\longrightarrow0,
 \qquad a_{n^2}=1.
\]
The same issue can be expressed by probability measures: take normalized volume measure except at square indices, where take a fixed point mass. For a continuous observable separating that point from its volume average, its errors behave exactly in this sparse way.
\paragraph{Source scope and gap.} These constructed measures are not claimed to be eigenfunction measures on a negatively curved manifold. They refute only the logical inference from averaged control to control of every eigenfunction, which is the source's explicit quantifier. Neither negative-curvature dynamics nor eigenfunction equations have been used to rule out the exceptional subsequence. The first gap is a uniform mechanism excluding every such concentration sequence. Spatial equidistribution and the stronger microlocal statement remain distinguished, and no arithmetic special-case theorem or current general status is asserted from memory.

